1
00:00:02,380 --> 00:00:03,680
Mr. Chairman is here.

2
00:00:17,660 --> 00:00:18,800
Welcome.

3
00:00:19,130 --> 00:00:20,430
Congratulations, sir.

4
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:22,770
Congratulations.

5
00:00:23,570 --> 00:00:24,740
Congratulations.

6
00:00:26,870 --> 00:00:28,040
Congratulations.

7
00:00:28,410 --> 00:00:30,340
- Congratulations. - Hello.

8
00:00:31,580 --> 00:00:32,940
- Congratulations, sir. - Congratulations, sir.

9
00:00:55,300 --> 00:00:57,940
The founder of Soonyang.

10
00:00:59,440 --> 00:01:01,940
It's him. Chairman Jin Yang Cheol.

11
00:01:04,280 --> 00:01:07,010
This is a dream. It can't be reality.

12
00:01:10,850 --> 00:01:12,550
He died 20 years ago.

13
00:01:19,990 --> 00:01:21,260
How could this be?

14
00:01:36,340 --> 00:01:37,380
Do Jun.

15
00:01:39,010 --> 00:01:40,350
Forgive me, Father.

16
00:01:54,630 --> 00:01:59,030
Do Jun. You must watch your manners when you're around Grandfather.

17
00:01:59,460 --> 00:02:02,370
He's young. It happens when you're overwhelmed.

18
00:02:03,030 --> 00:02:06,240
I'll watch Do Jun. You can go on ahead.

19
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:07,410
Okay, then.

20
00:02:08,110 --> 00:02:09,370
You sweet boy.

21
00:02:13,480 --> 00:02:16,180
That's what your grandfather is like.

22
00:02:16,480 --> 00:02:18,950
Nothing about his life is fun.

23
00:02:19,550 --> 00:02:22,450
Would thorns break out on his hand...

24
00:02:22,490 --> 00:02:25,120
if he were to just stroke your head?

25
00:02:25,960 --> 00:02:29,230
Do Jun. Come with Grandma.

26
00:02:30,600 --> 00:02:33,500
- "Grandma?" - Yes, sweetie.

27
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:38,070
Who...

28
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:40,770
Who am I?

29
00:02:41,710 --> 00:02:42,940
You're so silly.

30
00:02:43,240 --> 00:02:46,780
What kind of question is that? You are Jin Do Jun,

31
00:02:47,180 --> 00:02:49,180
the youngest grandchild of the Soonyang family.

32
00:02:58,390 --> 00:03:00,560
(The 24th Trade Day Business Medal Reward Ceremony)

33
00:03:02,030 --> 00:03:06,130
It's the year 1987?

34
00:03:08,270 --> 00:03:11,670
I'm a member of Chairman Jin Yang Cheol's family?

35
00:03:13,170 --> 00:03:14,270
The youngest?

36
00:03:15,210 --> 00:03:16,470
This can't be.

37
00:03:18,980 --> 00:03:20,950
(The 24th Seoul Olympic Games)

38
00:03:20,950 --> 00:03:24,950
(Reborn Rich)

39
00:03:25,280 --> 00:03:27,620
(Episode 2)

40
00:03:30,790 --> 00:03:33,660
Hyeong Jun, Do Jun, it's your first visit, isn't it?

41
00:03:35,760 --> 00:03:37,360
This is Grandpa's place.

42
00:03:37,530 --> 00:03:40,100
Whoa. Is this the main entrance?

43
00:03:40,630 --> 00:03:42,130
It's massive.

44
00:03:42,170 --> 00:03:43,300
It's just the same.

45
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:47,870
Jeongsimjae, the Soonyang residence that was theirs for generations.

46
00:03:49,610 --> 00:03:51,180
A monk well-versed in geomancy...

47
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:54,550
picked out the auspicious spot for a home and told Chairman Jin...

48
00:03:55,880 --> 00:03:59,650
as long as they were good at heart, money would never dry up.

49
00:04:01,350 --> 00:04:02,820
The name "Jeongsimjae..."

50
00:04:03,820 --> 00:04:05,790
literally means "rightful heart."

51
00:04:25,480 --> 00:04:27,610
Wow, this is amazing.

52
00:04:30,050 --> 00:04:32,850
One, two, three, four, five.

53
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:35,650
Gosh. How many rooms are there?

54
00:04:35,820 --> 00:04:36,990
Thirteen.

55
00:04:38,590 --> 00:04:40,930
What? How do you know that?

56
00:04:41,430 --> 00:04:43,760
Have you been here without me?

57
00:04:44,660 --> 00:04:46,030
Don't be silly.

58
00:04:46,930 --> 00:04:49,400
Hyeong Jun, you promised Mom.

59
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:50,970
That you'll be a good boy today.

60
00:04:51,600 --> 00:04:52,600
Yes.

61
00:04:53,970 --> 00:04:55,140
Do Jun, you too.

62
00:04:56,680 --> 00:04:57,980
Don't get too nervous.

63
00:04:58,240 --> 00:05:00,680
It looks like you're nervous.

64
00:05:01,880 --> 00:05:02,910
What?

65
00:05:04,680 --> 00:05:08,150
Let's go. Grandma and Grandpa will be waiting.

66
00:05:10,420 --> 00:05:11,420
Come along.

67
00:05:22,730 --> 00:05:27,010
Bells toll and flowers are in bloom

68
00:05:27,040 --> 00:05:31,240
Birds sing and people smile

69
00:05:31,240 --> 00:05:35,580
I miss you, my love

70
00:05:35,580 --> 00:05:39,120
Please do not leave my side

71
00:05:39,350 --> 00:05:43,220
Where we first met and fell in love

72
00:05:43,590 --> 00:05:47,590
The sweet roads I gave my heart to

73
00:05:47,860 --> 00:05:51,960
In beautiful Seoul

74
00:05:51,960 --> 00:05:56,670
I want to live in Seoul

75
00:06:12,450 --> 00:06:15,850
However busy you are, the meat and fish cannot be cold.

76
00:06:15,850 --> 00:06:18,860
Reheat and reserve every now and then.

77
00:06:24,430 --> 00:06:26,930
- Do not scrimp on the salt. - I understand.

78
00:06:27,100 --> 00:06:30,000
People these days eat less salt to stay healthy,

79
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:31,970
but food must be seasoned enough.

80
00:06:32,170 --> 00:06:34,340
Don't worry about that, Mother.

81
00:06:34,540 --> 00:06:36,640
Your first daughter-in-law has it under control.

82
00:06:37,610 --> 00:06:41,080
I'll teach my sister-in-law how we do things.

83
00:06:41,110 --> 00:06:42,380
Don't worry, okay?

84
00:06:44,580 --> 00:06:46,920
My husband handpicked...

85
00:06:46,920 --> 00:06:50,320
Soonyang Hotel's best cooks and waiting staff.

86
00:06:50,320 --> 00:06:53,190
Don't worry about anything and stay by Father's side.

87
00:06:53,290 --> 00:06:54,730
You're the guest of honour.

88
00:06:55,030 --> 00:06:58,930
It's your father-in-law's birthday, and he's the one who won the medal.

89
00:06:59,030 --> 00:07:00,570
How am I the guest of honour?

90
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:01,670
Don't say that.

91
00:07:04,100 --> 00:07:07,040
Soonyang owes its immense growth to you, Mother.

92
00:07:07,240 --> 00:07:09,910
Who doesn't know that?

93
00:07:10,240 --> 00:07:13,340
That's such a sweet way of telling me to stop nagging...

94
00:07:13,510 --> 00:07:14,980
and get out of the kitchen.

95
00:07:17,350 --> 00:07:18,720
Hello, Hae In.

96
00:07:21,990 --> 00:07:25,190
What should I do, Mother?

97
00:07:25,990 --> 00:07:28,360
Don't you even think of doing anything.

98
00:07:28,860 --> 00:07:31,260
Stay with Yoon Ki and the boys.

99
00:07:34,530 --> 00:07:36,840
- Mother, leave it to us. - Okay.

100
00:07:36,870 --> 00:07:38,170
Go on.

101
00:07:39,940 --> 00:07:41,570
Do you want me...

102
00:07:41,610 --> 00:07:43,780
- to prepare the fruit? - Mr. Ko, get the fruit.

103
00:07:43,810 --> 00:07:45,010
Yes, ma'am.

104
00:07:45,980 --> 00:07:47,350
They're gutsy.

105
00:07:47,910 --> 00:07:50,920
He cut contact to marry a woman his parents disapproved of.

106
00:07:50,950 --> 00:07:53,050
They then showed up after ten years...

107
00:07:53,120 --> 00:07:55,490
to laugh and smile and enjoy having a family.

108
00:07:56,990 --> 00:07:59,620
I'm incapable of putting on such an act.

109
00:07:59,860 --> 00:08:01,730
She's not like us at all.

110
00:08:02,730 --> 00:08:04,560
She was an actress.

111
00:08:05,100 --> 00:08:07,100
She doesn't suit this family.

112
00:08:07,500 --> 00:08:08,970
She belongs on stage.

113
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:11,100
Right?

114
00:08:14,370 --> 00:08:16,840
Are you being bullies now because you weren't in school?

115
00:08:17,210 --> 00:08:20,610
You have way too many wrinkles by your eyes.

116
00:08:21,480 --> 00:08:23,280
- Ms. Ye Jun. - What are you doing?

117
00:08:24,720 --> 00:08:27,120
When so many people are present?

118
00:08:28,690 --> 00:08:29,850
Ms. Lee.

119
00:08:32,890 --> 00:08:35,130
Don't try to play a daughter-in-law...

120
00:08:35,660 --> 00:08:36,860
and stick to what you did.

121
00:08:37,400 --> 00:08:40,400
Stand still like a portrait and smile prettily.

122
00:08:42,300 --> 00:08:43,400
You're good at that.

123
00:08:59,250 --> 00:09:00,520
Happy birthday, sir.

124
00:09:02,220 --> 00:09:03,250
Happy birthday, sir.

125
00:09:04,320 --> 00:09:05,460
Let's have a drink.

126
00:09:06,090 --> 00:09:08,460
- Happy birthday. - Happy birthday, sir.

127
00:09:13,830 --> 00:09:15,370
He studied in Tokyo...

128
00:09:15,970 --> 00:09:18,840
and works as a master at a sushi restaurant in Ginza.

129
00:09:19,870 --> 00:09:22,670
The Japanese refused to let him go,

130
00:09:22,710 --> 00:09:25,010
but I literally abducted him and got him...

131
00:09:25,010 --> 00:09:27,980
on an early flight so he could cater to you today.

132
00:09:29,350 --> 00:09:30,380
It's good, isn't it?

133
00:09:30,880 --> 00:09:31,950
Yes.

134
00:09:32,050 --> 00:09:33,150
I knew it.

135
00:09:33,620 --> 00:09:36,890
Domestic goods still can't compare to Japanese.

136
00:09:40,730 --> 00:09:41,760
How many?

137
00:09:43,390 --> 00:09:45,960
Grains of rice. How many are there?

138
00:09:46,360 --> 00:09:49,570
The ideal weight of fish and rice is 15g...

139
00:09:49,600 --> 00:09:50,600
So how many?

140
00:09:52,240 --> 00:09:54,970
- I apologize, sir. - There are 320.

141
00:09:56,140 --> 00:09:57,840
A trained sushi master...

142
00:09:58,910 --> 00:10:02,580
usually picks up 320 grains of rice to make one piece.

143
00:10:03,010 --> 00:10:05,720
That many might be appropriate for lunch,

144
00:10:06,620 --> 00:10:09,520
but on a day like this, or when served with alcohol,

145
00:10:10,860 --> 00:10:13,390
use just 280 grains of rice, okay?

146
00:10:14,960 --> 00:10:15,990
So it's not too filling.

147
00:10:16,860 --> 00:10:18,100
I'll do that, sir.

148
00:10:23,400 --> 00:10:25,240
Cheongwadae sent a messenger, sir.

149
00:10:28,970 --> 00:10:31,040
- The Blue House? - Yes.

150
00:10:45,360 --> 00:10:46,360
Sir.

151
00:10:46,590 --> 00:10:48,060
- Happy birthday. - Happy birthday.

152
00:10:48,130 --> 00:10:50,190
Thank you. Eat your fill.

153
00:10:50,230 --> 00:10:51,260
- Thank you. - Thank you.

154
00:10:54,870 --> 00:10:58,200
Father. How did you know the number of rice grains?

155
00:10:59,740 --> 00:11:02,610
Is there a Japanese restaurant in Soonyang Hotel, yes or no?

156
00:11:02,940 --> 00:11:04,110
Of course...

157
00:11:04,110 --> 00:11:06,410
There. Must I say more?

158
00:11:10,580 --> 00:11:11,650
Hey, you.

159
00:11:12,150 --> 00:11:15,620
Deputy CEO of Soonyang Electronics. Tell me.

160
00:11:16,490 --> 00:11:18,260
What is this year's sales?

161
00:11:18,990 --> 00:11:20,590
It's 2.3 billion dollars.

162
00:11:20,590 --> 00:11:22,630
- Up by 15 percent... - And the Japanese?

163
00:11:22,630 --> 00:11:26,130
H made 26.5 billion dollars, and T made 20 billion dollars.

164
00:11:26,700 --> 00:11:28,300
Both more than ten times we did.

165
00:11:28,330 --> 00:11:30,700
Our deputy CEO is right, then.

166
00:11:31,370 --> 00:11:33,500
We still can't compare to the Japanese.

167
00:11:35,810 --> 00:11:36,810
Is that true?

168
00:11:36,940 --> 00:11:38,740
Still, we're number one in our country.

169
00:11:39,140 --> 00:11:40,850
We never lost...

170
00:11:40,850 --> 00:11:43,610
the top spot in Korea in the white goods market.

171
00:11:43,610 --> 00:11:45,920
The top spot in Korea.

172
00:11:47,290 --> 00:11:48,290
The top spot in Korea?

173
00:11:49,920 --> 00:11:51,690
Are you competing in a national competition?

174
00:11:58,530 --> 00:11:59,560
Father.

175
00:12:01,300 --> 00:12:03,300
Yoon Ki wishes to say hello.

176
00:12:07,570 --> 00:12:10,440
Congratulations on winning a medal and happy birthday, Father.

177
00:12:11,940 --> 00:12:15,510
He opened a film distribution company.

178
00:12:15,610 --> 00:12:18,280
His first movie will be shown this year.

179
00:12:18,550 --> 00:12:20,420
Aren't you proud of him?

180
00:12:20,420 --> 00:12:22,620
He did it all without your help.

181
00:12:23,550 --> 00:12:26,060
He'll do well. He's your son.

182
00:12:27,290 --> 00:12:31,400
He said he'll visit every weekend like the others.

183
00:12:32,060 --> 00:12:33,260
If you permit it.

184
00:12:33,830 --> 00:12:38,140
He did a great job raising both boys.

185
00:12:38,340 --> 00:12:41,410
Hyeong Jun, Do Jun, come and meet your grandfather.

186
00:12:43,410 --> 00:12:44,440
Bow.

187
00:12:45,080 --> 00:12:46,340
Yes, Father.

188
00:12:46,740 --> 00:12:48,480
Don't be so angry with him.

189
00:12:48,510 --> 00:12:50,010
Do movies make money, mister?

190
00:12:51,680 --> 00:12:53,380
Something more valuable than money...

191
00:12:53,380 --> 00:12:54,920
Will it help Soonyang?

192
00:12:55,650 --> 00:12:57,390
- Father. - It makes no money...

193
00:12:57,420 --> 00:12:58,890
and won't help Soonyang.

194
00:13:00,160 --> 00:13:01,660
Why are you my son?

195
00:13:04,660 --> 00:13:06,760
- Honey. - Guests are leaving.

196
00:13:08,530 --> 00:13:09,630
Throw salt after them.

197
00:13:15,370 --> 00:13:16,870
It really is a party.

198
00:13:17,180 --> 00:13:19,280
There are beggars everywhere.

199
00:13:23,380 --> 00:13:25,880
He doesn't mean what he says.

200
00:13:30,860 --> 00:13:33,220
Yoon Ki, you know what your father's like.

201
00:13:34,290 --> 00:13:36,560
Don't take it to heart, okay?

202
00:13:37,760 --> 00:13:39,860
Yes. Leave it at that today.

203
00:13:39,860 --> 00:13:41,330
Let's take it slowly.

204
00:13:42,300 --> 00:13:43,300
Let's go and eat.

205
00:13:43,430 --> 00:13:44,900
You eat lots.

206
00:13:48,070 --> 00:13:49,870
He married against his parents' will,

207
00:13:50,370 --> 00:13:53,110
so 4-0's right to succession was revoked.

208
00:13:53,140 --> 00:13:54,250
Hello.

209
00:13:54,950 --> 00:13:57,580
That's exactly what I know.

210
00:14:17,200 --> 00:14:18,300
But...

211
00:14:23,880 --> 00:14:24,940
I'm missing.

212
00:14:27,350 --> 00:14:30,450
I know all there is to know about Soonyang's Jin family.

213
00:14:31,080 --> 00:14:32,150
But...

214
00:14:32,320 --> 00:14:34,290
(Late Jin Yang Cheol, Late Lee Pil Ok)

215
00:14:34,550 --> 00:14:36,850
(Jin Yoon Ki, Lee Hae In, Jin Hyeong Jun)

216
00:14:40,420 --> 00:14:44,000
I have no information on 4-2 Jin Do Jun.

217
00:14:46,130 --> 00:14:47,160
Why...

218
00:14:47,630 --> 00:14:51,640
is my mind blank when it comes to 4-2 Jin Do Jun?

219
00:14:53,910 --> 00:14:54,910
Why is that?

220
00:15:02,280 --> 00:15:04,150
You know, sir,

221
00:15:04,150 --> 00:15:06,650
how the great 6.29 Declaration came to be.

222
00:15:07,290 --> 00:15:12,160
It was all thanks to the President's concern and thoughtfulness.

223
00:15:13,620 --> 00:15:15,190
History will record him...

224
00:15:15,430 --> 00:15:18,400
as the father of democracy in our land.

225
00:15:21,770 --> 00:15:22,830
Try the tea.

226
00:15:24,300 --> 00:15:25,400
It smells lovely.

227
00:15:30,540 --> 00:15:31,680
In the next administration,

228
00:15:33,340 --> 00:15:36,410
shouldn't the average man take the lead role?

229
00:15:38,520 --> 00:15:40,380
History is marching on,

230
00:15:40,990 --> 00:15:42,620
and Soonyang should join the flow.

231
00:15:44,960 --> 00:15:48,430
The President wishes to give you an opportunity.

232
00:15:57,030 --> 00:15:58,170
Mr. Lee.

233
00:15:58,800 --> 00:15:59,800
Yes, sir.

234
00:16:01,770 --> 00:16:03,040
Were you aware?

235
00:16:04,780 --> 00:16:08,650
This gentleman from the Blue House knew.

236
00:16:16,090 --> 00:16:18,860
This medal you see here.

237
00:16:20,620 --> 00:16:21,790
The payment is deferred.

238
00:16:24,560 --> 00:16:26,230
He's here to collect.

239
00:16:29,630 --> 00:16:30,630
So,

240
00:16:34,340 --> 00:16:36,570
how much do you want for it?

241
00:16:51,890 --> 00:16:56,790
Your window just won't open

242
00:16:57,630 --> 00:17:02,030
I'll knock on it with the moonlight of love

243
00:17:04,500 --> 00:17:05,500
Jeez...

244
00:17:18,320 --> 00:17:22,850
Oh, my love

245
00:17:23,220 --> 00:17:26,460
Open the window to let in the breeze

246
00:17:26,490 --> 00:17:27,490
Shoot.

247
00:17:48,210 --> 00:17:49,680
Vice-Chairman Jin Seong Jun?

248
00:17:58,060 --> 00:18:00,060
It's obvious what movies make money.

249
00:18:00,590 --> 00:18:02,690
- HongKongers shooting guns. - "A Better Tomorrow?"

250
00:18:02,690 --> 00:18:04,960
- Or Americans going to war. - "Platoon."

251
00:18:05,630 --> 00:18:07,060
So what kind of movie are you making?

252
00:18:07,870 --> 00:18:10,130
It's about the French people praying.

253
00:18:10,530 --> 00:18:12,070
It's called "Under the Sun of Satan."

254
00:18:12,540 --> 00:18:15,370
I thought you wanted to make a movie, not build a hotel.

255
00:18:16,040 --> 00:18:17,480
Do you want to make everyone fall asleep?

256
00:18:19,440 --> 00:18:21,750
Dad! Do Jun is in trouble.

257
00:18:22,210 --> 00:18:23,210
He's upstairs now.

258
00:18:34,230 --> 00:18:36,860
You broke this vase. Okay, kiddo?

259
00:18:38,330 --> 00:18:40,260
We're the only ones in this room right now.

260
00:18:40,760 --> 00:18:44,340
No matter what you say, everyone will believe me.

261
00:18:45,970 --> 00:18:48,840
Why? Because I'm the rightful heir to the throne,

262
00:18:49,170 --> 00:18:51,040
and Grandpa will side with me no matter what.

263
00:19:03,590 --> 00:19:04,660
Did you just scoff?

264
00:19:05,020 --> 00:19:07,190
You were a real mess even when you were young.

265
00:19:08,360 --> 00:19:10,900
What? Have you lost your mind?

266
00:19:10,900 --> 00:19:12,030
Seong Jun!

267
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:19,070
- Hey. My gosh, are you all right? - What happened?

268
00:19:19,070 --> 00:19:21,110
- Do you know how much this costs? - Are you okay?

269
00:19:21,110 --> 00:19:23,240
Father absolutely treasures this porcelain vase.

270
00:19:24,580 --> 00:19:25,910
It was him.

271
00:19:25,940 --> 00:19:29,210
He broke it. He tried to run away, but I caught him.

272
00:19:29,710 --> 00:19:31,350
- Oh, dear. - Do Jun.

273
00:19:32,680 --> 00:19:34,550
Is that true?

274
00:19:37,390 --> 00:19:39,420
Hold on. Yoon Ki.

275
00:19:40,290 --> 00:19:42,030
This is making me very uncomfortable.

276
00:19:42,030 --> 00:19:46,100
Are you implying that Seong Jun could be lying?

277
00:19:46,530 --> 00:19:48,370
How could you accuse Seong Jun of lying...

278
00:19:48,370 --> 00:19:51,070
He is lying.

279
00:19:51,500 --> 00:19:53,900
What? What do you mean?

280
00:19:54,310 --> 00:19:55,540
The vase...

281
00:19:59,540 --> 00:20:00,880
He's the one who broke it.

282
00:20:03,710 --> 00:20:05,980
He was trying to steal the chairman's belonging.

283
00:20:06,680 --> 00:20:08,090
I caught him in the act.

284
00:20:24,870 --> 00:20:26,700
He got flustered and tried to run away, but...

285
00:20:27,500 --> 00:20:28,640
- Hey! - No!

286
00:20:29,240 --> 00:20:31,080
- Seong Jun! - Do Jun.

287
00:20:31,280 --> 00:20:32,440
- Are you all right? - What is going on?

288
00:20:34,210 --> 00:20:36,310
- Father. - Seong Jun...

289
00:20:37,720 --> 00:20:39,250
It wasn't me, Grandpa.

290
00:20:39,280 --> 00:20:41,550
- I didn't break it. I swear... - Enough.

291
00:20:43,850 --> 00:20:45,220
Shut your mouth.

292
00:20:51,460 --> 00:20:52,960
This happened in 1987,

293
00:20:53,730 --> 00:20:55,930
at the 60th birthday party for your grandfather,

294
00:20:55,930 --> 00:20:57,300
former Chairman Jin.

295
00:20:58,570 --> 00:21:00,200
Year 1987.

296
00:21:01,370 --> 00:21:02,940
Chairman Jin Yang Cheol.

297
00:21:06,240 --> 00:21:07,280
And his 60th birthday party.

298
00:21:07,280 --> 00:21:10,680
You smashed the Goryeo celadon that he cherished...

299
00:21:11,480 --> 00:21:14,390
and was scolded by him for the first time.

300
00:21:15,350 --> 00:21:16,520
The smashed vase?

301
00:21:18,620 --> 00:21:19,720
Seong Jun.

302
00:21:21,030 --> 00:21:22,990
Do you know what you did wrong?

303
00:21:26,030 --> 00:21:27,030
Come here.

304
00:21:30,200 --> 00:21:31,300
Sit down.

305
00:21:38,480 --> 00:21:42,150
You see, I don't care about this vase.

306
00:21:43,510 --> 00:21:47,050
Seong Jun, you will continue my legacy...

307
00:21:47,580 --> 00:21:50,250
and become the owner of Soonyang in the future.

308
00:21:51,460 --> 00:21:52,490
Okay?

309
00:21:54,730 --> 00:21:56,760
Everything you say...

310
00:21:57,700 --> 00:21:59,460
and do...

311
00:22:00,660 --> 00:22:02,700
could make or break ten thousand employees' livelihoods.

312
00:22:04,540 --> 00:22:07,770
Even their families' livelihoods will depend on you.

313
00:22:12,840 --> 00:22:16,350
Yet you can't even keep your emotions under control?

314
00:22:16,880 --> 00:22:18,420
Acting up like this...

315
00:22:22,290 --> 00:22:23,350
It wasn't an adequate quality...

316
00:22:24,320 --> 00:22:25,460
"Isn't an adequate quality..."

317
00:22:26,520 --> 00:22:27,690
isn't an adequate quality...

318
00:22:28,530 --> 00:22:31,330
"in someone who will run a business that is Soonyang."

319
00:22:32,500 --> 00:22:35,170
in someone who will run a business...

320
00:22:36,500 --> 00:22:38,140
that is Soonyang.

321
00:22:41,310 --> 00:22:43,770
What I read in his autobiography is unfolding before my eyes.

322
00:22:44,140 --> 00:22:45,840
It was white porcelain.

323
00:22:48,010 --> 00:22:50,380
My grandfather's vase that I broke.

324
00:22:51,480 --> 00:22:53,980
It wasn't Goryeo celadon. It was a white porcelain vase.

325
00:23:01,830 --> 00:23:03,060
Everything is happening...

326
00:23:03,630 --> 00:23:07,030
exactly as I know it.

327
00:23:20,940 --> 00:23:22,850
The past as I know it.

328
00:23:23,910 --> 00:23:26,580
I'm in Korea in Year 1987.

329
00:23:29,620 --> 00:23:30,750
Then...

330
00:23:32,620 --> 00:23:33,820
If that's the case...

331
00:23:33,820 --> 00:23:36,060
(Jeongsimjae)

332
00:23:50,110 --> 00:23:52,440
(Three Way Restaurant)

333
00:23:59,320 --> 00:24:00,880
That was a great meal. Let's go.

334
00:24:07,390 --> 00:24:09,490
- Thank you. - Did you enjoy the food?

335
00:24:09,490 --> 00:24:12,100
- Yes. - Get back safely.

336
00:24:12,100 --> 00:24:13,260
Hyeon Min?

337
00:24:35,990 --> 00:24:37,050
Mom.

338
00:24:47,530 --> 00:24:49,500
(Ajin Motors)

339
00:24:49,930 --> 00:24:52,070
- Hyeon Min! - You're here.

340
00:24:52,070 --> 00:24:53,270
Dad!

341
00:24:53,600 --> 00:24:54,910
Hi, Hyeon Min!

342
00:24:55,010 --> 00:24:58,210
Lucky you, Hyeon Min! Daddy picked up fried chicken for you.

343
00:24:58,240 --> 00:24:59,710
Who do you like more? Mommy or Daddy?

344
00:25:00,240 --> 00:25:01,380
Mommy!

345
00:25:02,550 --> 00:25:03,980
- I knew it! - I'll do better.

346
00:25:04,010 --> 00:25:05,650
- Do you need a hand? - No, I'm good.

347
00:25:05,680 --> 00:25:07,550
Come on. Let's have this fried chicken.

348
00:25:15,590 --> 00:25:17,490
We found Do Jun.

349
00:25:18,800 --> 00:25:20,560
We'll get there soon too.

350
00:25:21,630 --> 00:25:23,030
Thank you, Mr. Oh.

351
00:25:24,030 --> 00:25:25,040
Okay.

352
00:25:27,270 --> 00:25:29,310
Do Jun is okay. You can put your worries to rest now.

353
00:25:31,740 --> 00:25:32,880
Thank goodness.

354
00:25:36,480 --> 00:25:37,580
Hello...

355
00:25:42,690 --> 00:25:45,960
Are you here alone? Your parents aren't here with you?

356
00:25:49,690 --> 00:25:52,860
Can I have one serving of gukbap?

357
00:25:55,470 --> 00:25:58,440
Sure. You can take that table over there.

358
00:26:57,960 --> 00:26:59,030
Hello...

359
00:26:59,760 --> 00:27:00,860
Do Jun.

360
00:27:06,700 --> 00:27:08,310
What are you doing here?

361
00:27:08,710 --> 00:27:09,970
I was so worried.

362
00:27:13,040 --> 00:27:15,350
Get up. Let's go.

363
00:27:16,510 --> 00:27:17,910
Let's go home.

364
00:27:20,180 --> 00:27:21,250
Let's...

365
00:27:22,450 --> 00:27:23,890
talk at home.

366
00:27:25,120 --> 00:27:26,220
Okay?

367
00:27:51,010 --> 00:27:54,850
(Daeil Bandage)

368
00:28:03,490 --> 00:28:04,560
What's wrong, Do Jun?

369
00:28:05,560 --> 00:28:06,660
What is it?

370
00:28:10,070 --> 00:28:11,370
I'm relieved.

371
00:28:14,770 --> 00:28:16,440
Mom's alive.

372
00:28:18,780 --> 00:28:20,540
I'm so relieved.

373
00:28:27,580 --> 00:28:28,850
Mom's relieved too.

374
00:28:30,550 --> 00:28:32,260
Thank goodness...

375
00:28:34,690 --> 00:28:36,330
I have you.

376
00:28:38,960 --> 00:28:40,100
Don't cry.

377
00:28:53,440 --> 00:28:56,510
That poor thing must've been so scared. Look how he ran away.

378
00:28:59,380 --> 00:29:00,750
Well done.

379
00:29:02,090 --> 00:29:05,460
Way to go.

380
00:29:07,720 --> 00:29:11,860
Your son and grandsons came to see you after ten years.

381
00:29:11,860 --> 00:29:14,100
How could you read a book after kicking them out like that?

382
00:29:14,970 --> 00:29:17,030
My son and grandsons? Who?

383
00:29:18,070 --> 00:29:20,700
I only scolded my eldest grandson,

384
00:29:21,000 --> 00:29:22,410
Seong Jun. No one else.

385
00:29:22,940 --> 00:29:25,910
You can't expect all your children to be the same.

386
00:29:25,940 --> 00:29:29,150
Let at least one of them do what they want.

387
00:29:29,150 --> 00:29:31,180
I fed them and paid for their education,

388
00:29:31,210 --> 00:29:32,280
so I must get my money's worth.

389
00:29:32,980 --> 00:29:35,120
I never invest in things where I can't get my money's worth.

390
00:29:37,450 --> 00:29:40,060
You'd better not coddle Yoon Ki.

391
00:29:44,290 --> 00:29:45,500
The others will turn out like him.

392
00:30:05,420 --> 00:30:09,190
The only person in this family who I know nothing about...

393
00:30:09,690 --> 00:30:12,790
is me, 4-2 Jin Do Jun.

394
00:30:14,360 --> 00:30:17,890
Am I living as Jin Do Jun now because I'm possessed?

395
00:30:17,890 --> 00:30:20,030
(Three Way Restaurant)

396
00:30:26,500 --> 00:30:27,470
(Three Way Restaurant)

397
00:30:27,800 --> 00:30:31,140
- Mom. - Hi, son!

398
00:30:31,140 --> 00:30:32,410
Hey, you. Come here.

399
00:30:32,440 --> 00:30:35,080
- Oh, look at you. - Gosh, stop!

400
00:30:35,080 --> 00:30:37,980
- Run! Go! - Hey, where are you going?

401
00:30:38,010 --> 00:30:41,750
- Oh, nice one. - Let's cheer for your brother!

402
00:30:42,120 --> 00:30:45,560
- Nice. - Well done.

403
00:30:46,620 --> 00:30:47,990
Or did I simply travel back in time?

404
00:30:48,990 --> 00:30:51,130
If not that... Have I been reincarnated?

405
00:30:52,030 --> 00:30:53,300
How did this happen?

406
00:30:54,360 --> 00:30:55,830
(Daily Schedule, Timetable)

407
00:31:01,400 --> 00:31:02,710
Why are you still up?

408
00:31:03,610 --> 00:31:04,640
It's getting late.

409
00:31:08,210 --> 00:31:11,550
Do Jun, what happened today... It must've been a lot for you.

410
00:31:24,860 --> 00:31:26,000
At first,

411
00:31:27,030 --> 00:31:28,800
I felt the same way.

412
00:31:30,300 --> 00:31:32,300
"What am I doing here?"

413
00:31:32,800 --> 00:31:35,270
"I don't belong in this world."

414
00:31:36,540 --> 00:31:40,140
I couldn't understand them. It was very frustrating.

415
00:31:41,240 --> 00:31:43,350
You felt the same way?

416
00:31:45,720 --> 00:31:46,750
Does that mean...

417
00:31:46,780 --> 00:31:49,890
It felt so foreign to me. I was scared,

418
00:31:50,520 --> 00:31:51,520
and it was uncomfortable.

419
00:31:52,460 --> 00:31:56,230
I almost regretted marrying your dad.

420
00:31:59,060 --> 00:32:01,770
But now, it's not so bad.

421
00:32:04,530 --> 00:32:09,940
I've found a reason to accept them as my family.

422
00:32:11,270 --> 00:32:12,840
A reason to accept them as your family?

423
00:32:13,340 --> 00:32:16,280
You and Hyeong Jun.

424
00:32:17,710 --> 00:32:18,980
Do Jun.

425
00:32:20,080 --> 00:32:23,650
I'm certain that you'll find your reason too, one day.

426
00:32:43,440 --> 00:32:46,140
All the companies are dropping their prices for their 64K DRAMs.

427
00:32:47,740 --> 00:32:50,010
Soonyang Semiconductor started exporting them this month.

428
00:32:51,210 --> 00:32:53,280
Japan and the US are already dominating the market.

429
00:32:53,280 --> 00:32:55,590
So if they're charging less than half of what we're asking for,

430
00:32:56,050 --> 00:32:58,790
Soonyang Semiconductor will not survive in the market, sir.

431
00:33:02,290 --> 00:33:03,330
What time is it now...

432
00:33:04,630 --> 00:33:05,760
in New York?

433
00:33:07,630 --> 00:33:08,770
It's 9pm, sir.

434
00:33:08,970 --> 00:33:11,070
Is Im Pil Sung in New York now?

435
00:33:11,070 --> 00:33:12,940
I'll tell him to give you a call at once.

436
00:33:12,970 --> 00:33:14,470
No, don't wake him up.

437
00:33:16,110 --> 00:33:18,070
Just tell him to fax it over when he wakes up.

438
00:33:18,740 --> 00:33:20,910
- Fax? What do you need, sir? - His resignation letter.

439
00:33:21,340 --> 00:33:22,410
Pardon me?

440
00:33:28,790 --> 00:33:31,890
I didn't know that I had a knife held to my throat...

441
00:33:31,890 --> 00:33:33,890
until I read that newspaper.

442
00:33:37,190 --> 00:33:38,600
Do you think it's acceptable?

443
00:33:41,530 --> 00:33:43,470
Did he go to the US to eat hamburgers?

444
00:33:44,930 --> 00:33:46,700
I'm done paying for his hamburgers.

445
00:33:49,510 --> 00:33:50,710
I saw the news, Father.

446
00:33:50,740 --> 00:33:54,540
The American companies slashed their price from 3 to 1.80 dollars.

447
00:33:54,940 --> 00:33:57,350
And the Japanese companies said they'd sell it for 0.30 dollars.

448
00:33:58,420 --> 00:34:00,780
If we sell ours at the price the Japanese companies are offering,

449
00:34:01,050 --> 00:34:04,150
we'll lose 130 million dollars this year alone.

450
00:34:04,990 --> 00:34:06,260
We're like the shrimp...

451
00:34:06,260 --> 00:34:08,390
getting squashed between two whales that are fighting.

452
00:34:08,490 --> 00:34:09,530
The semiconductor business...

453
00:34:10,990 --> 00:34:12,100
Let's just give up here.

454
00:34:12,900 --> 00:34:14,430
I'm afraid we've come too far.

455
00:34:14,600 --> 00:34:15,670
The initial investment alone...

456
00:34:15,670 --> 00:34:17,600
Right, so let's cut our losses and call it quits.

457
00:34:19,040 --> 00:34:20,970
Let's stop trying to fill the bottomless pit.

458
00:34:21,910 --> 00:34:23,870
Youngjin Semiconductor has given up too.

459
00:34:24,570 --> 00:34:26,510
They're being sold to a Japanese company.

460
00:34:28,410 --> 00:34:31,280
Think of the question you always ask us.

461
00:34:32,280 --> 00:34:33,950
Will the semiconductor business bring in money?

462
00:34:37,220 --> 00:34:39,820
(Jeongsimjae)

463
00:34:44,830 --> 00:34:47,260
What brings you by at this hour?

464
00:34:47,660 --> 00:34:50,700
I'm sorry for causing you concern yesterday.

465
00:34:56,010 --> 00:34:58,040
I'm here to apologize to Grandpa.

466
00:34:59,180 --> 00:35:03,510
Look at you talking like a grown man. You're so mature.

467
00:35:04,080 --> 00:35:06,680
Come with me. He's upstairs in his study.

468
00:35:07,180 --> 00:35:08,220
Come on.

469
00:35:14,820 --> 00:35:16,890
Kids should behave like kids.

470
00:35:17,490 --> 00:35:20,930
Is she naive? Or is she becoming dense?

471
00:35:21,560 --> 00:35:23,830
- Hey. - I'm talking about Mother.

472
00:35:24,030 --> 00:35:25,030
Oh.

473
00:35:25,840 --> 00:35:27,200
Isn't it so obvious?

474
00:35:27,370 --> 00:35:30,140
Clearly, he memorized what his father told him to say.

475
00:35:30,370 --> 00:35:31,770
He's talking like a man in his 40s.

476
00:35:34,940 --> 00:35:36,410
Wait here.

477
00:35:36,710 --> 00:35:39,080
He'll be out soon.

478
00:35:39,780 --> 00:35:41,280
You can watch TV if you get bored.

479
00:35:41,580 --> 00:35:42,620
- Okay. - All right, then.

480
00:35:48,290 --> 00:35:49,490
("Two Kims Continue to Disagree on Single Candidacy")

481
00:35:49,890 --> 00:35:51,490
("Last Minute Conflict Surrounding Single Candidacy")

482
00:35:59,870 --> 00:36:01,640
You should deliver the campaign fund yourself...

483
00:36:01,970 --> 00:36:04,370
and meet him in person.

484
00:36:04,670 --> 00:36:05,680
What?

485
00:36:06,810 --> 00:36:08,810
The general election will take place in April next year.

486
00:36:09,750 --> 00:36:10,910
You need a nomination.

487
00:36:12,780 --> 00:36:16,090
Oh, right. Honey, you know everything.

488
00:36:16,090 --> 00:36:17,850
You sure take after Father.

489
00:36:23,660 --> 00:36:25,400
I heard you had visitors from Cheongwadae yesterday.

490
00:36:26,160 --> 00:36:28,430
Did they ask you to back Roh Tae Woo's campaign?

491
00:36:32,140 --> 00:36:35,910
Mr. Lee only listens and never spills what he hears.

492
00:36:36,710 --> 00:36:39,380
I'm your daughter, Father. Of course, I know that much.

493
00:36:39,580 --> 00:36:40,910
You silly goose.

494
00:36:41,510 --> 00:36:42,650
Take a seat.

495
00:36:43,680 --> 00:36:44,810
You too.

496
00:36:46,880 --> 00:36:48,790
Instead of calling you to Cheongwadae,

497
00:36:49,050 --> 00:36:52,620
they came all the way here. It means the tables have turned.

498
00:36:53,490 --> 00:36:55,590
It tells me that Roh Tae Woo is at a disadvantage.

499
00:36:55,630 --> 00:36:58,160
I'm not surprised. After all the protests and uprisings...

500
00:36:58,160 --> 00:37:00,500
to end the military dictatorship,

501
00:37:00,530 --> 00:37:02,770
who'd want to vote for another Military Academy graduate?

502
00:37:03,200 --> 00:37:05,700
Unless the entire nation is suffering from amnesia collectively.

503
00:37:05,970 --> 00:37:07,870
The two Kims will agree on single candidacy soon.

504
00:37:08,100 --> 00:37:10,270
The opposition power will win this time, Father.

505
00:37:10,270 --> 00:37:11,740
That being said,

506
00:37:12,140 --> 00:37:14,940
shouldn't you decide which candidate to support now?

507
00:37:15,350 --> 00:37:17,510
Between DJ and YS, choose the one who's more likely to win...

508
00:37:17,510 --> 00:37:20,950
Right. So who would that be?

509
00:37:21,180 --> 00:37:22,790
DJ, obviously.

510
00:37:23,050 --> 00:37:24,920
He is supported by all the student and civic groups...

511
00:37:24,950 --> 00:37:27,490
that helped establish the direct election system.

512
00:37:29,290 --> 00:37:31,590
Dong Ki, you should never get into politics.

513
00:37:31,890 --> 00:37:34,160
We should support YS, not DJ.

514
00:37:34,600 --> 00:37:36,600
I know DJ has many fans, but he also has many enemies.

515
00:37:36,600 --> 00:37:39,700
When it's a neck-and-neck fight, the one with less enemies will win.

516
00:37:41,000 --> 00:37:43,140
Aren't you saying that because you dislike DJ?

517
00:37:44,140 --> 00:37:46,080
I heard Kim Dae Jung was against...

518
00:37:46,080 --> 00:37:49,010
nominating Chang Je since he worked as a public security prosecutor.

519
00:37:50,180 --> 00:37:51,850
Why are you roping Chang Je into this?

520
00:37:52,180 --> 00:37:54,580
I am saying these things for the sake of the company's future.

521
00:37:56,050 --> 00:37:58,220
- Father! - Be quiet.

522
00:37:59,360 --> 00:38:01,790
I'm sorry for causing you concern, Father.

523
00:38:02,490 --> 00:38:04,290
- Mr. Lee. - Yes, sir.

524
00:38:04,290 --> 00:38:06,000
As for their approval ratings,

525
00:38:06,560 --> 00:38:08,700
get Soonyang Economic Research Institute to look into it.

526
00:38:09,770 --> 00:38:12,700
Tell them to find out which one of them deserves my money more.

527
00:38:12,940 --> 00:38:13,970
Yes, sir.

528
00:38:16,110 --> 00:38:17,470
Now, get out.

529
00:38:21,010 --> 00:38:23,510
- Oh. - Hey, aren't you Yoon Ki's son?

530
00:38:24,180 --> 00:38:27,480
I'm here to apologize to Grandpa for what happened yesterday.

531
00:38:28,890 --> 00:38:32,860
Oh, my. Yoon Ki always had a sly side to him.

532
00:38:33,390 --> 00:38:35,020
After not visiting us once for ten years,

533
00:38:35,020 --> 00:38:37,830
he now sends his son here every day.

534
00:38:38,390 --> 00:38:40,700
He came all the way here by himself because his parents told him to?

535
00:38:41,530 --> 00:38:42,870
He sure takes after his father.

536
00:38:43,530 --> 00:38:45,740
Good-looking and calculating.

537
00:38:47,970 --> 00:38:50,640
Your youngest son's child is here to see you, sir.

538
00:38:51,140 --> 00:38:53,410
I only have two sons. I didn't know I had another son!

539
00:38:54,640 --> 00:38:56,550
I will talk to him and send him home, sir.

540
00:39:00,080 --> 00:39:01,620
Come with us. Let's go downstairs.

541
00:39:03,720 --> 00:39:05,560
Please tell Grandpa...

542
00:39:06,620 --> 00:39:10,290
that I'm here to pay for the vase that broke yesterday.

543
00:39:11,390 --> 00:39:12,800
That punk.

544
00:39:12,830 --> 00:39:15,430
Hey! You little brat.

545
00:39:15,430 --> 00:39:19,440
Hey, do you even know how much that vase costs?

546
00:39:19,940 --> 00:39:21,100
Five bills?

547
00:39:21,700 --> 00:39:24,410
It can't cost more than that.

548
00:39:24,410 --> 00:39:26,810
Five bills? What? Five dollars?

549
00:39:27,510 --> 00:39:28,810
Or 50 dollars?

550
00:39:31,580 --> 00:39:32,680
No, five million dollars.

551
00:39:34,680 --> 00:39:36,550
What? Five million?

552
00:39:40,720 --> 00:39:43,790
Wouldn't that be enough to fund a presidential election campaign?

553
00:39:46,830 --> 00:39:48,160
What? Presidential election campaign?

554
00:39:50,700 --> 00:39:52,540
Please let Grandpa know.

555
00:39:53,200 --> 00:39:56,740
If it were me, I'd back Roh Tae Woo's campaign.

556
00:40:00,240 --> 00:40:03,080
Roh Tae Woo will become President.

557
00:40:06,180 --> 00:40:09,090
Did you eavesdrop on the adults' conversation?

558
00:40:10,220 --> 00:40:12,560
Clearly, your parents couldn't teach you any better.

559
00:40:13,060 --> 00:40:15,160
Is this how your parents taught you?

560
00:40:16,430 --> 00:40:19,500
No one teaches their children to be so brazen.

561
00:40:20,200 --> 00:40:22,530
Just like how no one tells their children...

562
00:40:22,670 --> 00:40:24,200
to steal their grandfather's things.

563
00:40:24,200 --> 00:40:25,870
- Do Jun. - What?

564
00:40:27,970 --> 00:40:30,110
Young Ki, you must be getting old.

565
00:40:30,370 --> 00:40:33,140
He's just a kid. Why are you getting so worked up?

566
00:40:33,510 --> 00:40:36,050
He's read some newspapers, so he's trying to sound like an adult.

567
00:40:36,650 --> 00:40:38,710
Once DJ and YS agree on single candidacy,

568
00:40:38,710 --> 00:40:40,620
Roh Tae Woo can't win.

569
00:40:40,620 --> 00:40:42,080
I assure you that he won't win.

570
00:40:42,550 --> 00:40:43,590
Single candidacy?

571
00:40:44,950 --> 00:40:47,890
Do you think the two of them will actually reach an agreement?

572
00:40:55,870 --> 00:40:57,100
I do not think so.

573
00:41:00,540 --> 00:41:02,610
Now, that should be enough to compensate him for the broken vase.

574
00:41:03,470 --> 00:41:05,580
I'll be off, then.

575
00:41:06,980 --> 00:41:08,010
Goodness.

576
00:41:10,580 --> 00:41:14,980
Oh, my. Yoon Ki did a great job, bringing up such a smart boy.

577
00:41:16,090 --> 00:41:17,220
Oh, sorry.

578
00:41:17,720 --> 00:41:18,790
Of course, it's nonsense.

579
00:41:19,060 --> 00:41:21,290
So many people are rooting for single candidacy.

580
00:41:21,290 --> 00:41:23,660
They won't betray the majority opinion.

581
00:41:23,990 --> 00:41:25,830
Both YS and DJ...

582
00:41:25,830 --> 00:41:28,660
have come this far because of their devotion...

583
00:41:28,930 --> 00:41:30,470
to the democratization of the nation.

584
00:41:31,430 --> 00:41:33,970
They won't gamble on their political careers.

585
00:41:35,240 --> 00:41:36,310
Exactly.

586
00:41:38,910 --> 00:41:41,910
Mr. Oh, take Mr. Chairman's grandson home.

587
00:41:44,580 --> 00:41:47,450
Sir, there's breaking news about the presidential election.

588
00:41:48,450 --> 00:41:50,090
You should see it.

589
00:41:50,790 --> 00:41:51,890
What's the matter?

590
00:41:53,920 --> 00:41:56,230
Kim Young Sam and Kim Dae Jung of the Democratic Party...

591
00:41:56,230 --> 00:42:00,000
decided against single candidacy earlier today.

592
00:42:00,100 --> 00:42:03,400
Kim Dae Jung clearly expressed...

593
00:42:03,430 --> 00:42:05,370
that he was against the party convention,

594
00:42:05,640 --> 00:42:08,910
which means they will both run for President.

595
00:42:08,910 --> 00:42:10,070
Father.

596
00:42:10,110 --> 00:42:12,540
Kim Young Sam and Kim Dae Jung met again...

597
00:42:12,540 --> 00:42:14,980
- Father! - to negotiate the details...

598
00:42:15,010 --> 00:42:16,810
regarding single candidacy but failed to reach an agreement.

599
00:42:17,080 --> 00:42:20,080
Their talk ended when they decided...

600
00:42:20,080 --> 00:42:23,020
to postpone the deadline to next Monday,

601
00:42:23,050 --> 00:42:24,850
which is when Kim Dae Jung would have to reply by.

602
00:42:26,620 --> 00:42:28,260
Wait, stop!

603
00:42:34,660 --> 00:42:36,570
Mr. Chairman would like to speak with you.

604
00:42:37,330 --> 00:42:38,430
Right now.

605
00:42:42,410 --> 00:42:43,470
Tell me.

606
00:42:45,170 --> 00:42:47,010
How did you know they'd decide against single candidacy?

607
00:42:48,080 --> 00:42:50,710
I wouldn't be able to concede. That's why.

608
00:42:51,110 --> 00:42:52,280
Because I'd get greedy.

609
00:42:53,280 --> 00:42:55,990
When three candidates are running for class president,

610
00:42:56,450 --> 00:42:58,550
the top two candidates will never join hands...

611
00:42:59,360 --> 00:43:01,720
because they both believe that they will win.

612
00:43:02,730 --> 00:43:06,200
Rather, they'll do whatever it takes to make each other lose.

613
00:43:06,660 --> 00:43:09,070
They'll bad-mouth each other and fight.

614
00:43:09,830 --> 00:43:12,700
Then their teachers and classmates...

615
00:43:13,200 --> 00:43:15,610
will realize that they, in fact, don't deserve the position.

616
00:43:16,310 --> 00:43:18,980
Just like that, they'll drag each other down.

617
00:43:19,040 --> 00:43:22,180
So the one who was least likely to win will end up winning.

618
00:43:23,010 --> 00:43:24,410
You mean he'll win by default.

619
00:43:25,180 --> 00:43:28,220
Roh Tae Woo will become President, by default.

620
00:43:28,620 --> 00:43:32,290
So I should back Roh Tae Woo. Is that right?

621
00:43:34,560 --> 00:43:37,990
If I were you, I'd give him the money before he became number one.

622
00:43:38,760 --> 00:43:42,100
A lot more than the amount he may be expecting.

623
00:43:43,430 --> 00:43:46,340
He'll be grateful if you give it to him when he's still number three.

624
00:43:46,840 --> 00:43:48,540
But if you wait until he becomes number one,

625
00:43:49,040 --> 00:43:51,040
he'll take it for granted.

626
00:43:59,280 --> 00:44:01,950
- Mr. Lee. - Yes, sir.

627
00:44:02,450 --> 00:44:04,990
Tell Mr. Oh to have the car ready.

628
00:44:05,620 --> 00:44:06,720
Yes, sir.

629
00:44:10,560 --> 00:44:13,500
- Hey. - Mr. Oh, have the car ready.

630
00:44:14,030 --> 00:44:15,830
Let me ask you one more question, then.

631
00:44:16,200 --> 00:44:19,470
I believe I've already paid you for the broken vase, Grandpa.

632
00:44:20,240 --> 00:44:22,470
It's nothing difficult. It's just a quiz.

633
00:44:22,610 --> 00:44:25,370
Then there must be a prize for getting it right.

634
00:44:25,740 --> 00:44:26,780
Because it's a quiz.

635
00:44:32,620 --> 00:44:34,550
I don't like to do things for free either.

636
00:44:37,120 --> 00:44:40,590
We talked about how number 3 can win by default because number 1 and 2...

637
00:44:40,620 --> 00:44:42,430
are busy fighting, right?

638
00:44:43,430 --> 00:44:44,990
But there's this saying too.

639
00:44:44,990 --> 00:44:47,700
"The shrimp is squashed to death when two whales fight."

640
00:44:49,270 --> 00:44:51,870
Then do you think there's a way...

641
00:44:53,040 --> 00:44:56,410
for the shrimp to beat the whales?

642
00:45:11,220 --> 00:45:13,220
You're just like other kids, after all.

643
00:45:27,100 --> 00:45:28,100
Hey.

644
00:45:29,110 --> 00:45:30,110
Come here.

645
00:45:36,750 --> 00:45:37,810
How did you know...

646
00:45:38,950 --> 00:45:40,520
the candidates won't be unified?

647
00:45:41,880 --> 00:45:42,990
Yoon Ki, no.

648
00:45:44,350 --> 00:45:46,060
Did your father tell you so?

649
00:45:50,560 --> 00:45:51,660
My brother said so.

650
00:45:52,560 --> 00:45:53,560
Your brother?

651
00:45:54,560 --> 00:45:56,170
This is what we do in times like these.

652
00:45:57,430 --> 00:46:00,200
"It's obvious at a single glance."

653
00:46:01,200 --> 00:46:02,300
What's with this punk?

654
00:46:02,400 --> 00:46:04,010
That's a buzzword by Hwang Ki Soon.

655
00:46:04,640 --> 00:46:05,640
Hwang Ki...

656
00:46:05,880 --> 00:46:07,910
You punk! That's not the way you should talk to your elders.

657
00:46:10,410 --> 00:46:13,680
Do you think there's a way for a shrimp to win against a whale?

658
00:46:14,680 --> 00:46:17,050
I guess you can't give up on the semiconductor, Chairman Jin.

659
00:46:19,620 --> 00:46:21,560
Why do you think I'm so set on semiconductor?

660
00:46:24,890 --> 00:46:29,270
Last summer, in Mokpo, Ulsan, and Changwon,

661
00:46:30,200 --> 00:46:33,040
when the labourers of our factories put on headbands...

662
00:46:33,800 --> 00:46:36,010
and stood there protesting...

663
00:46:36,540 --> 00:46:39,740
with cranes and excavators, asking me for a raise...

664
00:46:40,080 --> 00:46:41,310
and the formation of a labour union,

665
00:46:43,410 --> 00:46:46,520
I only thought about this...

666
00:46:48,780 --> 00:46:50,950
in my head.

667
00:46:54,060 --> 00:46:57,030
I am done doing business by using labourers.

668
00:46:58,060 --> 00:46:59,160
Then...

669
00:46:59,500 --> 00:47:00,500
From now on,

670
00:47:01,930 --> 00:47:04,070
we must do business with technologies to make a living.

671
00:47:07,470 --> 00:47:08,470
Semiconductor is...

672
00:47:09,410 --> 00:47:12,070
the future business of Soonyang.

673
00:47:14,240 --> 00:47:15,280
I see.

674
00:47:15,310 --> 00:47:16,910
Do you ask if it'll be worth any money?

675
00:47:21,450 --> 00:47:23,790
Am I the only one who sees this?

676
00:47:26,860 --> 00:47:29,530
Why is there nobody else who can think like this old man?

677
00:47:32,160 --> 00:47:34,130
We have to make an astronomical investment,

678
00:47:34,160 --> 00:47:35,760
but we do not know if it'll be a success.

679
00:47:36,770 --> 00:47:39,700
The semiconductor business is nothing but a risk,

680
00:47:40,240 --> 00:47:41,800
no, more like gambling at this point, Chairman Jin.

681
00:47:46,910 --> 00:47:48,180
Once our finances look better...

682
00:47:48,180 --> 00:47:50,910
by overseas construction business with the government's cooperation,

683
00:47:51,280 --> 00:47:53,920
why don't you resume the semiconductor business then?

684
00:47:54,720 --> 00:47:56,350
Do you know what democratization is?

685
00:47:57,950 --> 00:47:58,990
I'm not sure.

686
00:47:59,860 --> 00:48:03,930
Before, only a single soldier was after the money in my pocket.

687
00:48:05,090 --> 00:48:08,530
That turned into three civilians.

688
00:48:10,030 --> 00:48:11,200
That's democratization.

689
00:48:30,620 --> 00:48:31,990
(Best Taste! Best Quality!)

690
00:48:43,330 --> 00:48:44,830
Please give this to the president.

691
00:48:45,970 --> 00:48:48,100
That I believe he will surely put an end...

692
00:48:48,870 --> 00:48:50,810
to this era of military dictatorship.

693
00:48:52,270 --> 00:48:53,280
Thank you.

694
00:48:57,310 --> 00:48:58,910
(People's Hiking Club, 1987)

695
00:49:00,520 --> 00:49:04,250
Our chairman was touched deeply by your character...

696
00:49:04,950 --> 00:49:08,260
when you said you will not take any political retaliation.

697
00:49:14,260 --> 00:49:15,760
Please use this...

698
00:49:16,330 --> 00:49:19,130
for the sake of peace in Korea just as you wanted.

699
00:49:19,800 --> 00:49:21,640
The campaign of Roh Tae Woo of Democratic Justice Party was...

700
00:49:21,640 --> 00:49:23,510
held in the square in front of Gwangju Station.

701
00:49:23,970 --> 00:49:26,580
As soon as the campaign began at 2pm,

702
00:49:26,580 --> 00:49:30,310
young people and university students came out protesting...

703
00:49:30,410 --> 00:49:33,020
and chanting Kim Dae Jung's name.

704
00:49:33,020 --> 00:49:33,980
("Tear Gas Dropped During Roh Tae Woo's Speech")

705
00:49:44,490 --> 00:49:45,560
(October 1987, "Business Weekly")

706
00:49:45,560 --> 00:49:46,730
(Korea's Semiconductor in Crisis, Youngjin Semiconductor to Be Sold)

707
00:49:47,260 --> 00:49:50,400
We talked about how number 3 can win by default because number 1 and 2...

708
00:49:50,430 --> 00:49:51,870
are busy fighting, right?

709
00:49:52,130 --> 00:49:55,800
Then do you think there's a way...

710
00:49:56,310 --> 00:49:58,540
for the shrimp to beat the whales?

711
00:49:58,670 --> 00:50:01,240
("Small Korean Businesses Sacrificed in This Global Chicken Game")

712
00:50:02,140 --> 00:50:03,150
Small?

713
00:50:03,150 --> 00:50:04,780
Snack time.

714
00:50:04,810 --> 00:50:05,850
I finally realized...

715
00:50:06,220 --> 00:50:08,950
the answer to Chairman Jin Yang Cheol's quiz.

716
00:50:12,120 --> 00:50:15,220
Grandma, I have something I'd like to say to Grandpa.

717
00:50:15,720 --> 00:50:16,990
Is he home right now?

718
00:50:19,900 --> 00:50:21,560
He's on a business trip to Baghdad?

719
00:50:44,550 --> 00:50:46,660
Then when will he return?

720
00:50:50,790 --> 00:50:52,800
October 29th.

721
00:50:58,330 --> 00:50:59,540
By any chance,

722
00:51:00,470 --> 00:51:02,870
do you know what his flight number is?

723
00:51:12,610 --> 00:51:14,580
Okay. Thank you, Grandma.

724
00:51:14,850 --> 00:51:16,590
I'll call you again next time.

725
00:51:17,550 --> 00:51:18,620
Bye.

726
00:51:24,390 --> 00:51:25,660
CAL 828.

727
00:51:27,160 --> 00:51:28,860
The CAL incident of 1987.

728
00:51:28,860 --> 00:51:31,800
An aircraft with 95 passengers and 20 flight attendants...

729
00:51:31,830 --> 00:51:34,370
went missing above Yangon, Myanmar.

730
00:51:35,370 --> 00:51:38,370
Chairman Jin Yang Cheol will return to Seoul...

731
00:51:39,010 --> 00:51:40,810
on that very plane, CAL 828.

732
00:51:41,510 --> 00:51:45,910
At midnight in Korea, it will take off from Baghdad Airport,

733
00:51:47,620 --> 00:51:48,680
in three hours.

734
00:51:49,950 --> 00:51:52,450
I only have three hours of time...

735
00:51:54,260 --> 00:51:55,620
to save Chairman Jin Yang Cheol.

736
00:51:57,630 --> 00:52:00,560
So they refuse to accept the terms we suggested?

737
00:52:00,930 --> 00:52:04,170
If we press them by using the royal family, it can happen.

738
00:52:05,600 --> 00:52:06,700
The royal family again?

739
00:52:07,370 --> 00:52:09,300
The second son of the King, Prince Hussein,

740
00:52:09,300 --> 00:52:11,240
plans on visiting Abu Dhabi...

741
00:52:11,410 --> 00:52:13,040
on the same flight as us, CAL 828.

742
00:52:15,140 --> 00:52:18,850
Mr. Lee right here is telling me to do a sales pitch...

743
00:52:19,010 --> 00:52:21,850
even when I'm on my flight.

744
00:52:27,620 --> 00:52:28,560
(Korea Telecom)

745
00:52:37,530 --> 00:52:38,800
You have reached the customer service center.

746
00:52:38,830 --> 00:52:41,040
It's a bombing attack. We must stop this terrorist attack.

747
00:52:41,700 --> 00:52:42,740
A bombing attack?

748
00:52:42,740 --> 00:52:46,680
On flight CAL 828 from Baghdad Airport to Seoul,

749
00:52:46,680 --> 00:52:48,810
a North Korean agent will plant a bomb.

750
00:52:49,410 --> 00:52:51,680
If you aren't prepared, it will blow up in open waters...

751
00:52:52,310 --> 00:52:53,950
and kill two passengers.

752
00:52:53,950 --> 00:52:55,050
Hey, kid.

753
00:52:55,080 --> 00:52:57,890
A prank call on bombing attacks and abductions of an aircraft is...

754
00:52:57,890 --> 00:53:00,160
a crime you will be punished for and will have to pay for damages...

755
00:53:00,160 --> 00:53:02,760
- through a civil action. - It's not a prank. It's true.

756
00:53:02,760 --> 00:53:05,090
Hundreds of lives are in danger.

757
00:53:05,560 --> 00:53:07,560
You have to save them!

758
00:53:10,530 --> 00:53:12,630
Hello?

759
00:53:25,080 --> 00:53:26,110
Of course.

760
00:53:27,180 --> 00:53:28,880
No one will be able to believe me.

761
00:53:30,550 --> 00:53:32,290
And that I am from the future.

762
00:53:33,160 --> 00:53:35,120
That I already know everything that will happen...

763
00:53:36,790 --> 00:53:38,190
from now on.

764
00:53:40,760 --> 00:53:43,800
(Korea Telecom)

765
00:53:43,830 --> 00:53:47,470
It's even hard for me to believe everything that's happening now.

766
00:53:53,780 --> 00:53:56,180
Grandma, open the door, please.

767
00:53:56,910 --> 00:53:58,580
We have no time, Grandma!

768
00:53:59,210 --> 00:54:00,280
Grandma!

769
00:54:08,060 --> 00:54:09,990
- Bring him a blanket, please. - Yes.

770
00:54:10,760 --> 00:54:13,430
Goodness, what brings you here at this hour?

771
00:54:13,830 --> 00:54:16,700
Grandma, can you let me speak to Grandpa?

772
00:54:17,100 --> 00:54:18,870
There is something I must tell him.

773
00:54:19,430 --> 00:54:20,970
We have no time, Grandma.

774
00:54:22,500 --> 00:54:25,340
Chairman Jin is in a meeting with local Iraqi staff.

775
00:54:25,370 --> 00:54:27,810
I will pass on a message if you leave it with me.

776
00:54:28,010 --> 00:54:29,240
Yes, I am ready.

777
00:54:30,310 --> 00:54:34,350
I finally found out the answer to the quiz you asked, Grandpa.

778
00:54:35,350 --> 00:54:37,850
A way for a shrimp to beat the whales.

779
00:54:38,950 --> 00:54:42,620
Once you see this note, I believe that you will...

780
00:54:43,530 --> 00:54:44,660
change your flight.

781
00:54:52,330 --> 00:54:54,600
- Great work. - Great work.

782
00:54:57,970 --> 00:54:59,780
Did anyone call from Seoul?

783
00:55:01,010 --> 00:55:03,010
- No, nobody called. - Good.

784
00:55:04,150 --> 00:55:05,310
Where is it?

785
00:55:07,020 --> 00:55:08,350
Man, where did it go?

786
00:55:14,060 --> 00:55:15,490
- Mr. Kim. - Yes!

787
00:55:15,790 --> 00:55:17,390
- Did you lose something? - No!

788
00:55:19,330 --> 00:55:21,460
Check if anything is missing before we go to the airport.

789
00:55:21,460 --> 00:55:22,700
Yes, sir.

790
00:55:23,930 --> 00:55:25,130
Great work, sir.

791
00:55:28,970 --> 00:55:30,040
Where is this thing?

792
00:55:36,650 --> 00:55:37,680
Thank you.

793
00:55:53,500 --> 00:55:56,630
Next story. On October 6th, HHI-1200, embarked the equipment...

794
00:55:56,670 --> 00:56:00,600
to build the Korean Research Center and left for Antarctica from Ulsan.

795
00:56:01,970 --> 00:56:05,240
Yesterday night, I began to hate you

796
00:56:06,170 --> 00:56:09,180
After 94 days, the ship stopped momentarily...

797
00:56:09,180 --> 00:56:11,010
at Port Valparaiso, their last stopover.

798
00:56:11,680 --> 00:56:15,050
- I began to hate you - Do Jun was watching it first.

799
00:56:17,690 --> 00:56:20,020
- Darn it. - They will have arrived...

800
00:56:20,060 --> 00:56:21,960
- by next month at the latest... - I'm watching the news right now!

801
00:56:21,990 --> 00:56:23,930
on King George Island.

802
00:56:23,930 --> 00:56:24,930
Jin Do Jun.

803
00:56:24,930 --> 00:56:27,600
An aircraft with 95 passengers and 20 flight attendants...

804
00:56:27,600 --> 00:56:30,230
went missing above Yangon, Myanmar.

805
00:56:30,270 --> 00:56:34,200
The details of the accident is yet to be discovered.

806
00:56:34,440 --> 00:56:36,410
Let us report to you...

807
00:56:36,410 --> 00:56:39,780
the details we know so far along with the list of passengers.

808
00:56:39,780 --> 00:56:42,640
Let us connect to the reporter.

809
00:56:50,390 --> 00:56:52,120
Have you checked the list of passengers?

810
00:56:52,390 --> 00:56:53,620
Young Ki is on it.

811
00:56:56,160 --> 00:56:59,260
Yes, is that the final list of passengers...

812
00:57:00,260 --> 00:57:03,570
from Baghdad Airport?

813
00:57:13,680 --> 00:57:14,810
No, right?

814
00:57:17,080 --> 00:57:20,420
Your father wouldn't pass away in such vain.

815
00:57:24,390 --> 00:57:26,560
I'm... I'm sorry, Mother.

816
00:57:26,560 --> 00:57:29,660
Oh no, Mother! Mother!

817
00:57:29,660 --> 00:57:32,260
- Mother. - Mother! Oh no.

818
00:57:32,390 --> 00:57:34,660
Water, bring her some water!

819
00:57:34,660 --> 00:57:37,370
Goodness, Mother. You poor woman.

820
00:57:41,540 --> 00:57:44,770
Chairman Jin's autobiography did not mention the CAL incident.

821
00:57:45,970 --> 00:57:47,380
Then did something change...

822
00:57:48,580 --> 00:57:50,650
because I came here?

823
00:57:54,580 --> 00:57:55,950
Was I too late?

824
00:57:56,350 --> 00:57:58,220
If I had remembered a little earlier,

825
00:58:00,260 --> 00:58:02,320
could I have saved Chairman Jin?

826
00:58:05,330 --> 00:58:06,800
Get it together!

827
00:58:11,870 --> 00:58:14,640
- No! - No, Father!

828
00:58:18,410 --> 00:58:19,510
Father!

829
00:58:23,140 --> 00:58:24,180
Father.

830
00:58:24,850 --> 00:58:25,910
Father.

831
00:58:26,580 --> 00:58:28,180
- Father. - Father!

832
00:58:29,780 --> 00:58:31,350
Did someone die around here?

833
00:58:32,350 --> 00:58:33,920
Why are you all crying?

834
00:58:33,960 --> 00:58:37,730
Father, I checked the final list of passengers from Baghdad just now.

835
00:58:37,930 --> 00:58:40,430
So? Are you disappointed...

836
00:58:40,800 --> 00:58:41,860
that I came back alive?

837
00:58:41,860 --> 00:58:44,270
Don't say it like that, Father!

838
00:58:44,430 --> 00:58:46,200
Because of you, we were all just...

839
00:58:46,700 --> 00:58:49,300
Good grief. You were all worried for nothing.

840
00:58:50,370 --> 00:58:52,810
Your father is yet to become a ghost.

841
00:58:57,650 --> 00:59:01,320
Your mom's face is what looks like a ghost.

842
00:59:08,220 --> 00:59:10,090
There was a change in his schedule due to business,

843
00:59:10,130 --> 00:59:11,930
so he had to arrive in Seoul earlier.

844
00:59:12,390 --> 00:59:15,760
We switched to another flight at the stopover, Abu Dhabi,

845
00:59:17,570 --> 00:59:19,370
so we were able to avoid this disaster.

846
00:59:20,640 --> 00:59:21,840
Great job.

847
00:59:21,870 --> 00:59:24,110
- Father. - Father.

848
00:59:29,640 --> 00:59:30,950
Father.

849
00:59:34,980 --> 00:59:36,480
What a relief, Father.

850
00:59:37,550 --> 00:59:40,060
I heard you suddenly had a business in Seoul.

851
00:59:40,490 --> 00:59:43,330
I don't know whose business it is, but I'd like to go bow to them.

852
00:59:44,390 --> 00:59:46,030
It's Youngjin Semiconductor.

853
00:59:46,060 --> 00:59:47,560
They're selling the business, right?

854
00:59:48,060 --> 00:59:49,600
I hear they will do it soon.

855
00:59:50,330 --> 00:59:52,330
I bought it today.

856
00:59:53,440 --> 00:59:54,900
Youngjin Semiconductor.

857
00:59:54,900 --> 00:59:56,400
- What? - What?

858
00:59:56,400 --> 00:59:58,370
Wait, weren't you going to give up on the semiconductor business?

859
00:59:59,640 --> 01:00:02,910
Father, you're going to jump in on this fight of whales?

860
01:00:03,080 --> 01:00:05,510
I'm going to make the shrimp bigger...

861
01:00:06,510 --> 01:00:08,950
so that the shrimp won't die in a fight between whales.

862
01:00:09,580 --> 01:00:12,450
- Father. - No matter how long it takes...

863
01:00:12,620 --> 01:00:14,560
or how much I have to invest,

864
01:00:16,990 --> 01:00:20,260
I will make this shrimp as big as a whale.

865
01:00:20,500 --> 01:00:22,130
But Father, right now, it's not...

866
01:00:22,160 --> 01:00:24,100
I just came back from my death.

867
01:00:25,700 --> 01:00:29,000
Do you think there is anything I'll be afraid of?

868
01:00:52,160 --> 01:00:53,330
(Pending Approval)

869
01:01:02,500 --> 01:01:06,570
I finally found out the answer to the quiz you asked, Grandpa.

870
01:01:07,780 --> 01:01:10,410
A way for a shrimp to beat the whales.

871
01:01:11,150 --> 01:01:13,010
It's to make the shrimp bigger.

872
01:01:13,420 --> 01:01:15,580
Then it won't die in the midst of a whales' fight.

873
01:01:16,690 --> 01:01:20,220
If you do not give up, time will be on the shrimp's side.

874
01:01:21,620 --> 01:01:23,730
The proposal of the buyout of Youngjin Semiconductor...

875
01:01:24,130 --> 01:01:25,890
ends at 5pm on the 29th.

876
01:01:27,500 --> 01:01:28,930
Once you see this note,

877
01:01:29,560 --> 01:01:32,700
I believe that you will change your flight.

878
01:01:38,970 --> 01:01:40,040
Chairman Jin.

879
01:01:43,010 --> 01:01:45,310
Are we stopping over at Abu Dhabi?

880
01:01:45,610 --> 01:01:46,680
Yes.

881
01:01:49,080 --> 01:01:51,850
Find the earliest flight to Seoul.

882
01:02:26,390 --> 01:02:29,490
Congratulations, Mr. President.

883
01:02:35,560 --> 01:02:37,330
During your presidency,

884
01:02:38,730 --> 01:02:41,340
please allow Soonyang to monopolize...

885
01:02:42,700 --> 01:02:44,140
the semiconductor business.

886
01:02:48,510 --> 01:02:49,840
Thank you.

887
01:03:01,120 --> 01:03:02,390
Just as you said,

888
01:03:03,120 --> 01:03:06,190
I handed over the fund for the presidential election myself.

889
01:03:11,330 --> 01:03:12,430
Why did you...

890
01:03:13,970 --> 01:03:15,540
tell me to fund...

891
01:03:17,970 --> 01:03:20,310
the second and third runners who aren't going to make it?

892
01:03:21,240 --> 01:03:23,110
Once the first place graduates,

893
01:03:23,140 --> 01:03:25,410
there will come a day for the 2nd and 3rd to win.

894
01:03:31,990 --> 01:03:32,990
By any chance,

895
01:03:35,420 --> 01:03:37,490
do you know what the future holds?

896
01:03:48,040 --> 01:03:50,870
You knew the single candidacy will fall under.

897
01:03:53,740 --> 01:03:56,440
You knew Roh Tae Woo would be elected.

898
01:03:59,810 --> 01:04:00,920
And...

899
01:04:07,190 --> 01:04:08,890
(I finally found out the answer to the quiz you asked, Grandpa.)

900
01:04:15,430 --> 01:04:17,370
you knew CAL 828 will blow up.

901
01:04:20,800 --> 01:04:22,500
You knew everything.

902
01:04:25,010 --> 01:04:26,040
Is that true?

903
01:04:29,580 --> 01:04:30,750
Answer me!

904
01:04:45,890 --> 01:04:47,160
I did know.

905
01:04:51,870 --> 01:04:53,030
Not the future,

906
01:04:54,540 --> 01:04:56,470
but I knew what was in your heart.

907
01:05:00,140 --> 01:05:03,440
There is no way for a shrimp to win against whales.

908
01:05:04,950 --> 01:05:06,920
You gave me that quiz...

909
01:05:07,620 --> 01:05:09,850
trying to grasp for straws because you knew...

910
01:05:10,080 --> 01:05:11,620
your new attempt seemed reckless.

911
01:05:14,620 --> 01:05:15,890
You weren't looking for an answer.

912
01:05:16,720 --> 01:05:18,660
You were looking for approval and support.

913
01:05:21,430 --> 01:05:22,960
All I knew was...

914
01:05:24,070 --> 01:05:25,630
how you felt in your heart.

915
01:05:38,710 --> 01:05:41,420
Why is he seeing him alone in the study?

916
01:05:42,550 --> 01:05:44,350
I mean, without Mr. Lee.

917
01:05:45,250 --> 01:05:47,860
- What's with Father? - Tell me about it.

918
01:05:48,490 --> 01:05:50,020
That rarely happens for us too.

919
01:05:52,660 --> 01:05:53,800
Young Ki.

920
01:05:59,130 --> 01:06:00,940
You got the answer,

921
01:06:03,040 --> 01:06:04,370
so you deserve the prize.

922
01:06:07,080 --> 01:06:08,310
How much do you want?

923
01:06:08,640 --> 01:06:10,140
I don't need money.

924
01:06:12,510 --> 01:06:14,780
Once I am old enough to use that money,

925
01:06:15,020 --> 01:06:16,620
its monetary value would have dropped.

926
01:06:19,720 --> 01:06:20,720
Is that so?

927
01:06:21,290 --> 01:06:22,390
I'd like land.

928
01:06:23,260 --> 01:06:26,490
A place with lots of plants and trees.

929
01:06:34,370 --> 01:06:36,600
I like this area, right here.

930
01:06:41,380 --> 01:06:45,180
That land was used to make pottery. It's useless.

931
01:06:45,180 --> 01:06:47,050
(Map of Seoul)

932
01:06:47,050 --> 01:06:48,420
(Gyeonggi Province, Seongnam, Bundang-dong)

933
01:06:48,450 --> 01:06:49,950
Do you want the land in Bundang that badly?

934
01:06:54,290 --> 01:06:55,890
Let's see.

935
01:06:57,390 --> 01:06:58,760
How does 160,000m² sound?

936
01:06:59,290 --> 01:07:01,660
There is one more thing I'd like, Grandpa.

937
01:07:01,760 --> 01:07:03,930
I think I'm done paying you out.

938
01:07:08,800 --> 01:07:09,870
Then let's make it a deal.

939
01:07:17,750 --> 01:07:21,780
You need to have something that I do not have...

940
01:07:22,550 --> 01:07:23,850
for a deal to be made.

941
01:07:25,350 --> 01:07:27,390
Do you think there is anything I do not have?

942
01:07:28,220 --> 01:07:29,960
Because you can't buy this with money.

943
01:07:32,390 --> 01:07:36,500
I'll bring you something that the Soonyang family doesn't have.

944
01:07:39,530 --> 01:07:41,270
The acceptance letter to the most prestigious college,

945
01:07:41,300 --> 01:07:42,970
Seoul National University, School of Law.

946
01:07:53,610 --> 01:07:54,620
You're right.

947
01:07:56,550 --> 01:07:58,090
An acceptance letter, I cannot buy that.

948
01:08:00,420 --> 01:08:01,560
Can you do this?

949
01:08:05,560 --> 01:08:07,300
What can I give you in return?

950
01:08:13,800 --> 01:08:15,240
Gather round, everyone.

951
01:08:30,150 --> 01:08:31,190
Jeong Rae.

952
01:08:32,220 --> 01:08:33,250
Yes, Father.

953
01:08:33,720 --> 01:08:36,020
Starting with the family gathering this weekend,

954
01:08:36,560 --> 01:08:38,790
make sure you set out...

955
01:08:39,790 --> 01:08:41,930
enough utensils for Do Jun's family as well.

956
01:08:51,170 --> 01:08:52,370
Why won't you answer me?

957
01:08:53,210 --> 01:08:55,440
Every week?

958
01:08:56,140 --> 01:08:58,250
Do Jun here is my grandson.

959
01:09:00,010 --> 01:09:01,180
Do you understand now?

960
01:09:21,940 --> 01:09:22,970
Family.

961
01:09:26,340 --> 01:09:28,180
4-alpha was right.

962
01:09:29,640 --> 01:09:31,510
There must be a reason why I became this family.

963
01:09:34,020 --> 01:09:36,250
The reason why I became family with the Jins.

964
01:09:40,720 --> 01:09:41,820
Right here.

965
01:09:46,890 --> 01:09:48,400
One of these people...

966
01:09:53,830 --> 01:09:55,640
killed me.

967
01:10:14,760 --> 01:10:17,690
How do you feel about entering SNU's law program as the top?

968
01:10:17,730 --> 01:10:19,430
Tell us your secret.

969
01:10:19,430 --> 01:10:22,360
How did you get in as the top of the class?

970
01:10:22,430 --> 01:10:25,730
- Say something. - Please introduce yourself.

971
01:10:27,740 --> 01:10:28,770
Well.

972
01:10:29,970 --> 01:10:33,140
I'm sure you all know my name.

973
01:10:34,640 --> 01:10:36,440
So is this what you're looking for?

974
01:10:39,010 --> 01:10:41,720
Chairman Jin Yang Cheol's grandson,

975
01:10:43,180 --> 01:10:46,420
College of Law, the class of 1996. My name is Jin Do Jun.

976
01:10:47,560 --> 01:10:49,460
I was born as Jin Do Jun...

977
01:10:50,020 --> 01:10:52,260
not as spirit possession, time travelling,

978
01:10:52,930 --> 01:10:54,060
or reincarnation.

979
01:10:55,430 --> 01:10:58,570
This life is my opportunity.

980
01:10:59,030 --> 01:11:02,970
(Reborn Rich)

981
01:11:33,170 --> 01:11:34,840
Play. Have fun.

982
01:11:35,270 --> 01:11:37,570
Go on group blind dates, regular blind dates,

983
01:11:37,610 --> 01:11:39,340
casual dates, and go out with someone.

984
01:11:39,340 --> 01:11:40,570
We've met before, right?

985
01:11:41,510 --> 01:11:43,040
Did you meet her? When?

986
01:11:43,640 --> 01:11:44,710
In 20 years' time.

987
01:11:44,810 --> 01:11:46,210
Do Jun, you're back!

988
01:11:47,620 --> 01:11:50,380
Why does Father play favourites with the youngest, Do Jun?

989
01:11:50,380 --> 01:11:52,720
Do Jun has exchanged the money in the account into dollars.

990
01:11:53,020 --> 01:11:54,960
I'd like to invest in companies in the US.

991
01:11:55,090 --> 01:11:57,590
Never bet on things that you aren't sure about.

992
01:11:57,590 --> 01:11:58,960
I have a lot of money, Mr. Oh.

993
01:11:59,190 --> 01:12:00,290
There is a problem.

994
01:12:00,390 --> 01:12:01,800
Just why?

995
01:12:01,800 --> 01:12:03,260
It's a foreign investment company.

996
01:12:03,930 --> 01:12:04,970
Mr. Chairman...

997
01:12:04,970 --> 01:12:08,870
would like to pass Soonyang down to someone who is like him.

998
01:12:08,900 --> 01:12:10,710
Do you simply have good discernment?

999
01:12:11,270 --> 01:12:12,770
Or are you just lucky?

